# Personal Claude Code Preferences

> This file loads into Claude's context on **every request**. Keep it lean —
> move language-specific detail into rules files with `paths:` frontmatter
> so they only load when relevant.

## How Context Loading Works

```
Always loaded (every request):
  CLAUDE.md             ← this file — keep under ~500 lines
  rules without paths:  ← general/contributing.md, general/security.md

Loaded on demand (only when editing matching files):
  rules with paths:     ← golang/*.md, ruby/*.md, etc.
```

Put high-level preferences and commands here. Put detailed conventions in
rules files scoped with `paths:` frontmatter.

## Project Defaults

### Go
- Go 1.22+
- Standard library first, dependencies sparingly
- `gofmt` and `goimports` on save
- Table-driven tests

### Ruby
- Ruby 3.3+, Rails 8.0+
- RSpec + FactoryBot for testing
- Use `Time.current` not `Time.now`
- Thin controllers, service objects for business logic

## Workflow
- Always run tests before committing
- Follow conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`)
- Plan before implementing non-trivial features

## Common Commands

```bash
# Go
go test ./...
go vet ./...

# Ruby
bundle exec rspec
bundle exec rubocop
```

## Rules Reference

### Always-on (no paths: frontmatter — loaded every request)
- @rules/general/contributing.md — Git workflow, PRs, code review
- @rules/general/security.md — Security checklist

### Go (loaded only when editing Go files)
- @rules/golang/style.md — Naming, formatting
- @rules/golang/error-handling.md — Error patterns
- @rules/golang/testing.md — Table-driven tests, mocks
- @rules/golang/concurrency.md — Goroutines, channels, sync
- @rules/golang/project-structure.md — Package design, layout
- @rules/golang/dependencies.md — Stdlib first, recommended libs

### Ruby (loaded only when editing Ruby files)
- @rules/ruby/models.md — Model conventions, migrations
- @rules/ruby/services.md — Service objects, query objects
- @rules/ruby/testing.md — RSpec, factories, request specs
- @rules/ruby/api.md — API design, serializers, versioning
- @rules/ruby/performance.md — N+1, caching, background jobs
- @rules/ruby/security.md — Auth, authorization, SQL injection
- @rules/ruby/contributing.md — Ruby-specific workflow, CI

## Context Budget Tips

- **CLAUDE.md loads on every request.** Each line here costs context on every
  interaction. Ask: "Would removing this cause Claude to make mistakes?" If
  not, delete it or move it to a rules file.
- **Rules without `paths:` also load every request.** The `general/` rules
  have no frontmatter and are always present — keep them concise.
- **Rules with `paths:` are free until triggered.** Language-specific rules
  only load when Claude works on matching files. This is where detailed
  conventions belong.
- **Target ~500 lines or fewer for CLAUDE.md.** If it grows beyond that,
  Claude may start ignoring rules buried in the noise.
